# End-to-end demo of the Reviews microservice.
#
# Prerequisite: start the service with the demo profile, which seeds one
# track (conference 1, track 1) with two papers and stubs the external
# Users/Submissions microservices:
#
#   ./gradlew bootRun --args="--spring.profiles.active=demo"     (Unix)
#   .\gradlew.bat bootRun --args="--spring.profiles.active=demo" (Windows)
#
# Demo cast (seeded by the demo profile):
#   user 1 = PC chair (also a PC member)   users 2, 3, 4 = reviewers
#   user 5 = author of both papers         papers 1 and 2 = seeded submissions
#
# Run the requests top to bottom (IntelliJ HTTP client / VS Code REST Client).
# Every request authenticates by passing requesterID as a query parameter.

### 0. The track starts in the BIDDING phase (submission deadline already passed)
GET http://localhost:8080/conferences/1/tracks/1/phase?requesterID=1

### 1. The chair lists the papers submitted to the track
GET http://localhost:8080/conferences/1/tracks/1/papers?requesterID=1

### 2. A reviewer reads a paper's title and abstract before bidding
GET http://localhost:8080/papers/1/title-and-abstract?requesterID=2

### 3. Reviewers bid on paper 1 (CAN_REVIEW / NEUTRAL / NOT_REVIEW)
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/1/bids?requesterID=2
Content-Type: application/json

"CAN_REVIEW"

### 4.
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/1/bids?requesterID=3
Content-Type: application/json

"CAN_REVIEW"

### 5.
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/1/bids?requesterID=4
Content-Type: application/json

"NEUTRAL"

### 6. ... and on paper 2
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/2/bids?requesterID=2
Content-Type: application/json

"CAN_REVIEW"

### 7.
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/2/bids?requesterID=3
Content-Type: application/json

"NEUTRAL"

### 8.
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/2/bids?requesterID=4
Content-Type: application/json

"CAN_REVIEW"

### 9. The chair inspects all bids on paper 1
GET http://localhost:8080/papers/1/bids?requesterID=1

### 10. The chair closes bidding by moving the deadline into the past
###     (body is a Unix timestamp in milliseconds) -> track enters ASSIGNING
PUT http://localhost:8080/conferences/1/tracks/1/bidding-deadline?requesterID=1
Content-Type: application/json

1700000000000

### 11. Confirm the phase change
GET http://localhost:8080/conferences/1/tracks/1/phase?requesterID=1

### 12. The chair triggers automatic assignment: every paper gets the three
###     bidding reviewers with the smallest workload
PUT http://localhost:8080/conferences/1/tracks/1/automatic?requesterID=1

### 13. Who reviews paper 1?
GET http://localhost:8080/papers/1/assignees?requesterID=1

### 14. The chair finalises the assignments (requires >= 3 reviewers per
###     paper) -> track enters REVIEWING
POST http://localhost:8080/conferences/1/tracks/1/finalization?requesterID=1

### 15. Confirm the phase change
GET http://localhost:8080/conferences/1/tracks/1/phase?requesterID=1

### 16. A reviewer lists the papers assigned to them
GET http://localhost:8080/papers/by-reviewer?requesterID=2

### 17. Reviewer 2 submits a review for paper 1
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/1/reviews?requesterID=2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "confidenceScore": "EXPERT",
  "commentForAuthor": "Strong contribution, clear experiments.",
  "confidentialComment": "I checked the proofs, they hold.",
  "recommendationScore": "STRONG_ACCEPT"
}

### 18. Reviewer 3 submits a review for paper 1
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/1/reviews?requesterID=3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "confidenceScore": "KNOWLEDGEABLE",
  "commentForAuthor": "Good paper, minor presentation issues.",
  "confidentialComment": "Section 4 could be tighter but the results convince me.",
  "recommendationScore": "WEAK_ACCEPT"
}

### 19. Reviewer 4 submits the last review for paper 1 -> the paper
###     automatically enters the IN_DISCUSSION phase
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/1/reviews?requesterID=4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "confidenceScore": "BASIC",
  "commentForAuthor": "Convincing results on all six language pairs.",
  "confidentialComment": "Outside my core area, deferring on theory.",
  "recommendationScore": "WEAK_ACCEPT"
}

### 20. Confirm the paper phase (asked by an assigned reviewer)
GET http://localhost:8080/papers/1/reviews/phase?requesterID=2

### 21. During discussion, reviewer 3 comments on reviewer 2's review
POST http://localhost:8080/papers/1/reviews/by-reviewer/2/discussion-comments?requesterID=3
Content-Type: application/json

"I agree with the strong accept, the error-correction idea is novel."

### 22. The chair reads the discussion
GET http://localhost:8080/papers/1/reviews/by-reviewer/2/discussion-comments?requesterID=1

### 23. The reviews agree (all accept), so the chair finalises paper 1
###     -> status ACCEPTED, paper phase REVIEWED
POST http://localhost:8080/papers/1/reviews/finalization?requesterID=1

### 24. Reviewers reject paper 2
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/2/reviews?requesterID=2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "confidenceScore": "EXPERT",
  "commentForAuthor": "The comparison baselines are outdated.",
  "confidentialComment": "Misses all post-2020 work.",
  "recommendationScore": "STRONG_REJECT"
}

### 25.
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/2/reviews?requesterID=3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "confidenceScore": "KNOWLEDGEABLE",
  "commentForAuthor": "Results do not support the claims.",
  "confidentialComment": "Variance bars overlap everywhere.",
  "recommendationScore": "WEAK_REJECT"
}

### 26.
PUT http://localhost:8080/papers/2/reviews?requesterID=4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "confidenceScore": "KNOWLEDGEABLE",
  "commentForAuthor": "Interesting idea but the evaluation is too narrow.",
  "confidentialComment": "Only two benchmarks tested.",
  "recommendationScore": "WEAK_REJECT"
}

### 27. The chair finalises paper 2 -> REJECTED. All papers are now decided,
###     so the track reaches the FINAL phase
POST http://localhost:8080/papers/2/reviews/finalization?requesterID=1

### 28. Confirm: the track is FINAL
GET http://localhost:8080/conferences/1/tracks/1/phase?requesterID=1

### 29. The author checks the verdicts
GET http://localhost:8080/papers/1/status?requesterID=5

### 30.
GET http://localhost:8080/papers/2/status?requesterID=5

### 31. The author reads a review of their accepted paper; note that the
###     confidential reviewer comment is hidden from authors
GET http://localhost:8080/papers/1/reviews/by-reviewer/2?requesterID=5

### 32. The chair pulls the track analytics
GET http://localhost:8080/conferences/1/tracks/1/analytics?requesterID=1
